<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n95672" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπᾰδον-ίζω</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπάδων</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>make
			flaccid</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ τοῖς ὀδοῦσι . . τὰς τῆς πιμελῆς
					κτηδόνας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Sor.
					1.118
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph. in
			trans. sense, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. τὸν ἦχον</span>
			<i>curtail, cramp, emasculate</i> their sound, of the short
			vowels, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				<u>Comp.</u>
				14
			</span></i> (as 
				v.l. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπανίζει</span>
			).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
